{
  "id": "T-SHOPDAY-NORMAL",
  "title": "BATCH-26 FOLD 2 (B7) CONTROL: three game hours of the gym at NORMAL speed with both players standing inside it. No skip of any kind in the measured window - this is the row every other row is judged against: what a normal-speed day actually pays, how many bodies it holds, how many shoppers leave without paying. NO save.",
  "preconditions": "Reporter fixture session fx-hq1 (day 44, MERGED - vars.keepMerger true). Dev build with skipvote / skipstate / shopday / tilldupes / perf / skippace / enterbuilding / exitbuilding (BAMP_DEV). THE SHOP IS THE GYM at vars.shop, picked by t-shopday-pick: of the four player-owned customer shops it had by far the most shopper entries for the measured morning (gym 203, fast food 137, hairdresser 74, clothing 40, read on each shop's OWNING machine). ITS OWNER IS THE CLIENT, so Client1's machine runs its live customers and its till and is the machine whose numbers matter; the host stands inside the same gym and waits. The fixture loads at 17:38 with Client1 already inside a building, so both step outside for a setup skip to 10:45 the next morning - that skip is taken OUTDOORS in every leg, with no shop occupied, so it is identical whatever skip-shop mode the measured window uses. NOTHING IS SAVED. ORACLE NOTE: the NullReferenceException oracle carries the `(?<!swallowed )` lookbehind (as t-skippace-watch does) because fx-hq1 prints the mod's own '[Gley] swallowed NullReferenceException' traffic-collider diagnostic, which has nothing to do with this fold.",
  "instances": 2,
  "vars": {
    "clientPid": "Client1",
    "hostPid": "melaus",
    "session": "fx-hq1",
    "keepMerger": true,
    "shop": "60 ba:street_fifthavenue"
  },
  "oracles_absent": [
    "\\[TickIso\\]",
    "\\[Guard\\]",
    "(?<!swallowed )NullReferenceException"
  ],
  "oracles_report": [
    "\\[Rest\\] CONSENSUS",
    "\\[Rest\\] skip GOAL reached",
    "\\[SkipPace\\] ",
    "\\[CarStack\\] ",
    "\\[Customers\\] ",
    "\\[Perf/"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "host",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "join",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "hostload ${session}",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 4,
      "role": "both",
      "cmd": "mark TEST T-SHOPDAY-NORMAL START",
      "expect_result": "OK MARK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 5,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 32,
      "note": "both worlds settle before anything is measured"
    },
    {
      "seq": 6,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "status",
      "expect_result": "settled=True"
    },
    {
      "seq": 7,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "status",
      "expect_result": "settled=True"
    },
    {
      "seq": 8,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "pause off",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 9,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "pause off",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 10,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "exitbuilding",
      "abort_on_fail": false,
      "note": "fx-hq1 loads Client1 inside a building; report-only, an outdoor player only warns"
    },
    {
      "seq": 11,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "exitbuilding",
      "abort_on_fail": false
    },
    {
      "seq": 12,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 8
    },
    {
      "seq": 13,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "skiprate",
      "expect_result": "^OK skiprate rate=50 ",
      "note": "the SHIPPED rate is what is measured - read, not set, so a drift fails here"
    },
    {
      "seq": 14,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "skipvote 10:45",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipvote goal="
    },
    {
      "seq": 15,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "skipvote 10:45",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipvote goal=",
      "abort_on_fail": false,
      "expect_log": [
        {
          "role": "h",
          "regex": "\\[Rest\\] CONSENSUS \\(2/2\\)",
          "within_s": 60
        }
      ],
      "note": "the SETUP skip: 17:38 -> 10:45 next day, ~20 s at rate 50, taken outdoors"
    },
    {
      "seq": 16,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 40
    },
    {
      "seq": 17,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "skipstate",
      "expect_result": "active=False",
      "note": "the setup skip finished - every number below is measured in the morning it reached"
    },
    {
      "seq": 18,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "skipvote off",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipvote goal=-"
    },
    {
      "seq": 19,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "skipvote off",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipvote goal=-"
    },
    {
      "seq": 20,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 5
    },
    {
      "seq": 21,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "enterbuilding ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK enterbuilding",
      "note": "THE OWNER (Client1) STANDS IN HIS OWN GYM - his machine runs its live customers and its till"
    },
    {
      "seq": 22,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "enterbuilding ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK enterbuilding",
      "note": "the other player waits inside the same gym and does nothing else"
    },
    {
      "seq": 23,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 22,
      "note": "the floor fills at NORMAL speed - this is the 'before' every leg starts from"
    },
    {
      "seq": 24,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "pending=[1-9]",
      "capture": {
        "preLive": "live=(\\d+)",
        "preEntries": "entries=(\\d+)",
        "preDue": "due=(\\d+)",
        "preTill": "tillOrders=(\\d+)",
        "preRev": "paidRevenue=([0-9.]+)",
        "preCap": "cap=(-?\\d+)",
        "preMinMult": "minMult=([0-9.]+)"
      },
      "note": "THE FLOW PREMISE: shoppers are still due today at this shop. Without this the leg could 'pass' on a dead shop and the table would compare two zeros."
    },
    {
      "seq": 25,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "live=[1-9]",
      "note": "THE SECOND HALF OF THE PREMISE: bodies are really standing on the floor at normal speed before the window opens."
    },
    {
      "seq": 26,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "perf reset",
      "expect_result": "^OK perf"
    },
    {
      "seq": 27,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "perf reset",
      "expect_result": "^OK perf"
    },
    {
      "seq": 28,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday reset",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday reset"
    },
    {
      "seq": 29,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "shopday reset",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday reset"
    },
    {
      "seq": 30,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "skipstate",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipstate",
      "capture": {
        "startMin": "nowMin=([0-9.]+)"
      },
      "note": "the window's START clock in raw game-minutes - the end is compared against it"
    },
    {
      "seq": 31,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 30
    },
    {
      "seq": 32,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "minMult=1",
      "note": "THE RATE THE WAIT IS SIZED ON: GameManager.MinutesMultiplier read off the lever. 1 game-minute per real second means 3 game hours = 180 real seconds, which is what the six polls below add up to. If this reads anything else the leg fails here rather than measuring the wrong window."
    },
    {
      "seq": 33,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 30
    },
    {
      "seq": 34,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday"
    },
    {
      "seq": 35,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 30
    },
    {
      "seq": 36,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday"
    },
    {
      "seq": 37,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 30
    },
    {
      "seq": 38,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday"
    },
    {
      "seq": 39,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 30
    },
    {
      "seq": 40,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday"
    },
    {
      "seq": 41,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 30
    },
    {
      "seq": 42,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday",
      "note": "the third game hour has closed - the window is over"
    },
    {
      "seq": 43,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 60,
      "note": "THE DRAIN: 60 real seconds at normal speed so bodies mid-checkout when the window closed can finish, and a paced body that failed to restore would show up here"
    },
    {
      "seq": 44,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "skipstate",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipstate",
      "capture": {
        "endMin": "nowMin=([0-9.]+)"
      },
      "expect_gt": {
        "nowMin=([0-9.]+)": "${startMin}"
      },
      "note": "THE WINDOW REALLY RAN: the clock is past where it started"
    },
    {
      "seq": 45,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "skippace",
      "expect_result": "^OK skippace max=1000 now=1 scaledBodies=0",
      "note": "EVERY paced body was restored - the dictionary is empty and the pace reads 1 again"
    },
    {
      "seq": 46,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "skippace",
      "expect_result": "^OK skippace max=1000 now=1 scaledBodies=0"
    },
    {
      "seq": 47,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday",
      "capture": {
        "endEntries": "entries=(\\d+)",
        "endDue": "due=(\\d+)",
        "endWindow": "window=(\\d+)",
        "bodies": "bodies=(\\d+)",
        "maxBodies": "maxBodies=(\\d+)",
        "cap": " cap=(-?\\d+)",
        "completeOrders": "completeOrders=(\\d+)",
        "livePays": "livePays=(-?\\d+)",
        "unpaidExits": "unpaidExits=(\\d+)",
        "paperHours": "paperHours=(\\d+)",
        "paperCandidates": "paperCandidates=(\\d+)",
        "paperOrders": "paperOrders=(\\d+)",
        "capDrops": "capDrops=(\\d+)",
        "endTill": "tillOrders=(\\d+)",
        "endRev": "paidRevenue=([0-9.]+)"
      },
      "note": "THE OWNER'S TABLE ROW - every figure the fold is judged on, from the machine that holds this gym's books"
    },
    {
      "seq": 48,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "shopday ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK shopday",
      "capture": {
        "hostBodies": "bodies=(\\d+)",
        "hostMaxBodies": "maxBodies=(\\d+)",
        "hostUnpaid": "unpaidExits=(\\d+)"
      },
      "note": "the follower's view: his puppets are driven from the owner's stream, so a wild difference here is a sync problem, not an economy one"
    },
    {
      "seq": 49,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "tilldupes ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "dupes=0",
      "capture": {
        "tdOrders": "orders=(\\d+)",
        "tdDistinct": "distinct=(\\d+)",
        "tdLiveCompleted": "liveCompleted=(-?\\d+)",
        "tdPaidRev": "paidRevenue=([0-9.]+)"
      },
      "note": "NO ORDER REACHED THE TILL TWICE - the H-SKIPDOUBLE-1 invariant this fold must not break"
    },
    {
      "seq": 50,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "tilldupes ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "dupes=0"
    },
    {
      "seq": 51,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "perf",
      "expect_result": "^OK perf",
      "capture": {
        "cWorst": "worstMs=(\\d+)",
        "cAvg": "avgMs=([0-9.]+)",
        "cSpikes": "spikes=(\\d+)"
      }
    },
    {
      "seq": 52,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "perf",
      "expect_result": "^OK perf",
      "capture": {
        "hWorst": "worstMs=(\\d+)",
        "hAvg": "avgMs=([0-9.]+)",
        "hSpikes": "spikes=(\\d+)"
      }
    },
    {
      "seq": 53,
      "role": "both",
      "cmd": "mark TEST SHOPDAY END",
      "expect_result": "OK MARK"
    }
  ]
}
